2. Gyan Bharatam is a reason not to build a manuscript repository

This is probably the single largest strategic implication of current Indian infrastructure.

Gyan Bharatam now explicitly targets more than one crore manuscripts, a national digital repository, AI-assisted transcription, provenance infrastructure, APIs to national/international archives, volunteer networks, educational modules and VR/AR experiences.

Trying to compete with that by saying:

    “Pāṭala will digitize India and host all its manuscript images”

would be strategically stupid.

Instead:

Pāṭala becomes a demand and intelligence layer over the repository ecosystem.

That makes you complementary.
