HMML does not simply fly in and seize manuscripts. It works through local holding institutions, provides equipment/training/support, and pays local technicians to create preservation images; copies remain with the holding library and are also preserved by HMML.

The British Library's Endangered Archives Programme likewise already provides mature guidance for surveys, cataloguing, digitization, photography/scanning and preservation workflows.

Therefore don't build a giant in-house digitization operation.

